    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Descended from one of New York's original Dutch merchant families, Carter Vanderweyden was a successful Southern lawyer before unknowingly defending a Kindred client in a rigged court case; impressed by his discretion, the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.ZJx9H3XnU8yQGy9s]{Malkavian} Julius Abrogard Embraced him on the spot in 1951. Vanderweyden served as a @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla} ambassador to departing @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} during the Battle of New York and later as an informal advisor to Prince Calebros, earning a reputation for scrupulous fairness. Now that Calebros has stepped down, Vanderweyden is a leading contender for the princedom, viewing the throne as a return to his family's ancestral birthright &mdash; though rivals whisper about the black veins in his aura (suggesting diablerie during the battle, which he insists was sanctioned) and his recurring blackouts, during which he acts and speaks normally but retains no memory afterward.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>You view the princedom as a duty, not a prize, and you campaign accordingly &mdash; as a staunch defender of the Traditions and a stable @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla}. You worry, more than you let on, about what you might do or reveal during your blackouts.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Julius Abrogard. Generation 9th; black veins in his aura suggest diablerie during the Battle of New York, which he claims was sanctioned. Derangement: @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.derangements.JournalEntry.96c107ceb8714b9b]{Fugue} (periodic blackouts). Ratings above 5 from the original stat block have been capped to fit this system's 1-5 scale.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
